{
  "uid": "bench-absurd",
  "title": "Bench \u2014 Absurd",
  "description": "Per-engine view of the Absurd bench guest: queue depth, throughput, latency, footprint against its 768 MiB Incus cap, and whether the workers and the metrics plumbing are actually up.",
  "tags": [
    "bench",
    "engine",
    "absurd"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "schemaVersion": 41,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "ds",
        "label": "Datasource",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {
          "text": "bench-prometheus",
          "value": "bench-prometheus"
        },
        "hide": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Queue depth",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue depth by queue",
      "description": "absurd_queue_depth from the absurd-queue-metrics timer on bench-absurd (job=node, instance=bench-absurd:9100, node-exporter textfile collector). Absurd has no engine process, so depth is counted straight out of the queue tables in Postgres: it is the one queue-depth gauge in this bench that is correct by construction, reporting work waiting for a worker class whether or not any worker for that class exists. max by (queue) collapses any duplicate series carrying different collector labels.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "max by (queue) (absurd_queue_depth)",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Current depth per queue",
      "description": "Latest absurd_queue_depth per queue. Both bench queues (default, gpu) are written on every collection run, so a missing bar means the collector stopped rather than that a queue drained \u2014 check the Health row.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 25
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "max by (queue) (absurd_queue_depth)",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Total work waiting",
      "description": "Sum of absurd_queue_depth across all queues. Zero here is only meaningful when the queue-metrics timer is fresh \u2014 see Queue metrics staleness in the Health row.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 50
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(max by (queue) (absurd_queue_depth))",
          "legendFormat": "waiting",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Throughput",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Task rate (proxy)",
      "description": "PROXY, not a task counter: rate of committed transactions in the bench database, rate(pg_stat_database_xact_commit{datname=\"bench\"}[5m]) from the postgres_exporter. Absurd has no engine process and exports no throughput metric, but every task lifecycle step is a write to this database, so commit rate tracks task activity up to a constant factor. It also includes the workers' own polling transactions, so it has a non-zero floor while workers are running and idle.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(pg_stat_database_xact_commit{datname=\"bench\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "commits",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(pg_stat_database_xact_rollback{datname=\"bench\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "rollbacks",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Row writes in bench DB (proxy)",
      "description": "PROXY: rate of rows inserted, updated and deleted in the bench database from pg_stat_database. Task creation shows up as inserts, state transitions and heartbeats as updates, and the hourly absurd-cleanup timer as a delete spike. Reading these as task counts requires knowing how many rows a task lifecycle writes, so treat the shape rather than the absolute value.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 10
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(pg_stat_database_tup_inserted{datname=\"bench\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "inserted",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(pg_stat_database_tup_updated{datname=\"bench\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "updated",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(pg_stat_database_tup_deleted{datname=\"bench\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "deleted",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Backends on bench DB",
      "description": "pg_stat_database_numbackends{datname=\"bench\"} \u2014 open connections to the bench database. With no engine process, this is the census of everything talking to Absurd: the two worker units, Habitat, and the queue-metrics and cleanup timers while they run.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "pg_stat_database_numbackends{datname=\"bench\"}",
          "legendFormat": "backends",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Worker polling load",
      "description": "Rate of rows returned and fetched in the bench database. Absurd workers claim tasks by polling Postgres, so this is the cost side of the throughput proxy: it stays elevated on an idle engine and separates 'workers are looking for work' from 'work is being done', which the insert and update rates show.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 18
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(pg_stat_database_tup_returned{datname=\"bench\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "rows returned",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "rate(pg_stat_database_tup_fetched{datname=\"bench\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "rows fetched",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Latency",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Oldest pending task age",
      "description": "absurd_queue_oldest_pending_seconds per queue, from the absurd-queue-metrics timer: the age of the oldest task that is claimable but not yet claimed. This is the whole latency story Absurd exports \u2014 it has no execution-duration histogram, because there is no engine process to record one. A line climbing linearly means nothing is draining that queue; a sawtooth is normal claim latency.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 26
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "stepAfter",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "max by (queue) (absurd_queue_oldest_pending_seconds)",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Oldest pending now",
      "description": "Current absurd_queue_oldest_pending_seconds per queue. Absurd applies no scheduling timeout of any kind, so a large value here is a task waiting patiently, not a task about to be discarded.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 26
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 300
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 3600
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "max by (queue) (absurd_queue_oldest_pending_seconds)",
          "legendFormat": "{{queue}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 29,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Footprint",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 30,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RAM, % of Incus cap",
      "description": "Working set as a percentage of the guest's 768 MiB cap, measured two ways: the Incus metrics endpoint (100 * (1 - incus_memory_MemAvailable_bytes / incus_memory_MemTotal_bytes) for name=bench-absurd) and, as a cross-check, the same ratio from the guest's own node_exporter. bench-absurd is a NixOS guest, so both views exist and should track each other; a divergence means one of the two is measuring a different cgroup scope.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 35
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "dashed"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "guest view"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - incus_memory_MemAvailable_bytes{name=\"bench-absurd\"} / incus_memory_MemTotal_bytes{name=\"bench-absurd\"})",
          "legendFormat": "incus view",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes{instance=\"bench-absurd:9100\"} / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes{instance=\"bench-absurd:9100\"})",
          "legendFormat": "guest view",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 31,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU, % of one core",
      "description": "sum by (name) (rate(incus_cpu_seconds_total{name=\"bench-absurd\"}[5m])) * 100 from the Incus metrics endpoint, summed over the mode label, with the guest's own non-idle CPU fraction from node_cpu_seconds_total as a cross-check. 100 means one core fully busy.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 35
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "guest view"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (name) (rate(incus_cpu_seconds_total{name=\"bench-absurd\"}[5m])) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "incus view",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - sum(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{instance=\"bench-absurd:9100\",mode=\"idle\"}[5m])) / sum(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{instance=\"bench-absurd:9100\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "guest view",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "type": "gauge",
      "title": "RAM vs cap, now",
      "description": "Current working set as a percentage of the 768 MiB Incus cap for bench-absurd, from incus_memory_MemTotal_bytes minus incus_memory_MemAvailable_bytes.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 43
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 70
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showThresholdMarkers": true,
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${ds}"
          },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - incus_memory_MemAvailable_bytes{name=\"bench-absurd\"} / incus_memory_MemTotal_bytes{name=\"bench-absurd\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Guest memory detail",
      "description": "Absolute memory inside the bench-absurd guest from its node_exporter: MemTotal is the 768 MiB cap as the guest sees it, MemAvailable what is left, and Cached the page cache the Incus working-set figure charges to the container. Per-process breakdown is not available \u2014 the node_exporter processes collector is off on this guest, so there are no node_processes_* series to attribute RAM to individual worker units.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${ds}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 18,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 43
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
